#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""smartroom-release: update a SmartRoom room (Studio or Intel Mini) to a new
release, as a trial.

The design is ~/smartroom-rollback/DESIGN.md. A release is one tested image:
a btrfs root and the boot files that start it. An update never runs a package
upgrade on the live system. It writes the new release beside the running one,
boots it once, and keeps it only if the room proves healthy. Otherwise the
boot chain boots the previous release by itself.

  Studio: aura-try + Limine one-shot (U-Boot efivars) + Apple watchdog
  Mini:   Limine one-shot (NVRAM) + boot-try counting + iTCO_wdt/softdog

  smartroom-release status [--json]
  smartroom-release list [--json]
  smartroom-release update RELEASE [--reboot] [--unsigned]
  smartroom-release stage  RELEASE [--unsigned]     write the release, arm nothing
  smartroom-release arm [--reboot]                  arm the staged trial
  smartroom-release rollback [--reboot]             trial the previous release
  smartroom-release discard                         drop an unarmed or failed trial
  smartroom-release health-run                      the boot-time service
  smartroom-release build-release --id ID --out DIR [--source-subvol NAME]
                                  [--sign-key FPR]  make a release from this room
  smartroom-release build-release --id ID --out DIR --source-path SUBVOL --line LINE
                                  --uki-from F [--boot-from F] [--source-info K=V]...
                                                    make a release from an image root (build host)
  Every release root passes check-root before it is sent or signed.
  smartroom-release restore N [--no-reboot]         Room Controller contract
  smartroom-release migrate RELEASE [--reboot] [--unsigned] [--force]
                                  old Mini -> release trial (fallback = current @)
  smartroom-release migrate-check                   refuse safely if the room cannot move
  smartroom-release esp-migrate [--esp-hold DIR]    move ESP UKI store + ws13d hold into boot-store
  smartroom-release check-root [ROOT] [--json]      the root invariant (owners, system dirs, sudoers)
                                                    on a directory, a root.btrfs.zst, or /

RELEASE is a directory holding manifest.json (see README.md), or an https URL
of one. Nothing here asks a question. Exit status is non-zero on error; with
--json an error is {"error": {"code": ..., "message": ...}} on stdout.

How a trial is one-shot at every layer:
  Studio aura-try  ESP file aura-try ("armed", newline, path, newline). aura
                   marks it spent before it boots the path; 178 s watchdog.
  Limine           LoaderEntryOneShot picks the trial UKI / entry once.
  Mini             efivarfs NVRAM holds the one-shot (no ubootefi.var). The
                   health service opens /dev/watchdog (iTCO_wdt or softdog).
  kernel           trial cmdline has watchdog.handle_boot_enabled=0 so the
                   health service must feed the watchdog.
Everything the trial changes is beside what is configured. Mark-good is a
fixed list of steps whose only switch is one rename of limine.conf.
The last KEEP_GOOD (5) good releases stay on disk for manual restore.
"""
